Master / parent record that holds all common data shared across all variants of a product (name, description, category, costing, routes, etc.).
Key Functional Use Cases:

Define base product information used by all variants
Manage attributes and variant creation (size, color, etc.)
Set default sales/purchase behavior, taxes, and pricelists
Control inventory valuation, routes (MTO/MTS, manufacture, buy)
eCommerce product pages and descriptions
BOMs, suppliers, and costing at template level
Mass updates and reporting on product families

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread)
Key Fields:
name (char, required), default_code (base reference)
categ_id → product.category
type (product / consu / service)
sale_ok, purchase_ok, active
uom_id, uom_po_id
list_price, standard_price
attribute_line_ids → One2many to product.template.attribute.line
tag_ids → Many2many to product.tag
description_sale, description_purchase, image_1920
route_ids, seller_ids

Critical Hooks: create_variant_ids, _compute_price, onchange_categ_id, _get_variant_name
Security: product.group_product_manager + company rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
product template, product master, product form, base product, product.model, template product, product attributes, product family, non-variant product, product definition, product.template
Related Models (most joined):

product.product (child variants — most important)
product.category
product.attribute.line / product.attribute.value
product.pricelist.item
mrp.bom
product.supplierinfo
stock.quant (via variants)

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
product.template is Odoo’s master product model containing shared data (name, categ_id, type, uom, list_price, standard_price, description, routes, attributes, and tags) for a product family. It serves as the parent of all product.product variants and is the central definition point used by Sales, Purchase, Inventory, Manufacturing, eCommerce, and POS across the entire system.